# Normalise line endings repository-wide.
#
# Text files are stored and checked out with LF. Before this file the tree was mixed —
# layouts/index.html and layouts/partials/comments.html were CRLF while every other template
# was LF, and the two docs disagreed with each other — so touching a CRLF file rewrote the
# whole file in the diff. `text=auto eol=lf` fixes that at the source: git normalises on the
# way in, hands out LF, and nobody has to think about it again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats: never normalise, never try to diff them (a `.woff2` of 200 KB would
# otherwise show up as a conflict on every merge).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Generated files. Marked so GitHub collapses them in a diff and so tooling that reads
# .gitattributes (linters, coverage reports, code review) skips them.
package-lock.json linguist-generated
hugo_stats.json linguist-generated
